1
00:00:00,510 --> 00:00:01,870
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,640
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:05,710 --> 00:00:07,710
The phone is turned off.
You are being connected to...

5
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:08,710
(Episode 40)

6
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,400
Mr. Seo, what brings you here?

7
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,340
Ms. Joo, how are you here?

8
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:36,570
I'm just here to see someone.

9
00:00:38,140 --> 00:00:39,810
Are you meeting someone, too?

10
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:43,380
Yes.

11
00:00:44,780 --> 00:00:45,850
I see.

12
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:48,490
Then I'll see you at the office.

13
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:51,190
Yes, see you.

14
00:00:56,930 --> 00:01:00,430
I heard you've been helping
Ko Eun Seol on the Design Team.

15
00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:07,640
Sometime soon, the three of us
should get together.

16
00:01:23,860 --> 00:01:24,990
The phone is turned off.

17
00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:26,830
You are being connected
to voicemail.

18
00:01:42,070 --> 00:01:45,210
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

19
00:01:58,290 --> 00:02:01,990
It was as if she knew exactly
that I'd be there.

20
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:04,930
She didn't even seem surprised.

21
00:02:07,030 --> 00:02:09,870
Of all places and times,

22
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,100
I just happened
to run into Director Joo?

23
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:19,180
Director Joo has to know I've been
looking into her background.

24
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:23,880
Then was that smile from earlier...

25
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:26,650
supposed to be a warning?

26
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:30,420
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

27
00:02:30,490 --> 00:02:31,860
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

28
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,220
So with this month's sales,

29
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:35,260
have we reached half
of our quarterly goal?

30
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:38,430
This is all thanks
to your help, ma'am.

31
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,970
Oh, I hardly did anything.

32
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:43,540
If you ever need my help
in the future,

33
00:02:43,670 --> 00:02:44,900
just let me know.

34
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,800
Thank you.

35
00:02:47,410 --> 00:02:50,740
I'm always rooting for you,
Chief Cha.

36
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:53,950
It's not just because
you're my future son-in-law.

37
00:02:54,650 --> 00:02:56,950
I've always thought of you...

38
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:59,880
as very reliable and endearing.

39
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:05,690
Seeing you stay strong
through difficult times...

40
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:08,360
and take care of your sick parent...

41
00:03:09,590 --> 00:03:11,330
was truly wonderful to see.

42
00:03:12,830 --> 00:03:15,900
I wanted my daughter
to learn that from you.

43
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:19,970
Hae Ra may have her flaws,

44
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:22,770
but please guide her
when she's wrong...

45
00:03:23,070 --> 00:03:24,880
and stay by her side.

46
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:29,410
I'm far from perfect myself,
but I'll do my best.

47
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:32,520
And I am saying this out of concern,

48
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,720
but even though
I'm now in charge of Shoejoy,

49
00:03:36,190 --> 00:03:39,490
earning points with the CEO
is a completely different matter.

50
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:43,330
To become a son-in-law
acknowledged by your father-in-law,

51
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,360
you'll need to put in
quite a bit of effort.

52
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:49,100
I understand what you mean.

53
00:03:49,830 --> 00:03:51,100
My husband is also...

54
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:54,070
just a typical father
who adores his daughter.

55
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:58,480
If you cherish and care for Hae Ra
just a little more,

56
00:03:59,010 --> 00:04:01,650
you'll probably become
the perfect son-in-law.

57
00:04:10,990 --> 00:04:13,190
Ms. Joo, you called for me?

58
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,100
Something urgent has come up
that needs looking into.

59
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:18,900
What is it?

60
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:22,800
You know Team Leader Seo Hyun Jae
from the Legal Team, right?

61
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:25,300
Yes, I've run into him
in the hallway a few times.

62
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:28,340
He seemed quite close
with Ko Eun Seol.

63
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,180
Right, and that's the problem.

64
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,150
I told you before, didn't I?

65
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:35,910
Before Manager Na died,

66
00:04:36,710 --> 00:04:39,720
he tried to pin the murder
of Ko Eun Seol's mother on me.

67
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,750
Yes, I remember.

68
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,760
It seems...

69
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:45,460
while preparing
for Ko Eun Seol's retrial,

70
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:47,760
Mr. Seo dug into Manager Na's case.

71
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:51,000
He's probably looking for traces
of how Manager Na tried to frame me.

72
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:55,500
Secretary Choi, look into it.

73
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:57,700
Figure out
what Seo Hyun Jae's after.

74
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:01,810
If we leave it alone,
they'll piece together...

75
00:05:02,070 --> 00:05:03,370
the bait Manager Na left behind,

76
00:05:03,440 --> 00:05:05,180
and turn nothing into something.

77
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,310
Yes, I'll keep a close eye...

78
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:08,880
on Team Leader Seo from Legal.

79
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,680
To meet the schedule
for next season,

80
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:13,480
we need to hurry
and check the fabrics.

81
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:15,690
Who's going to inspect
the Cheonan Factory?

82
00:05:16,250 --> 00:05:17,320
That'll be me.

83
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:20,730
I heard the manager over
at that factory is quite difficult.

84
00:05:21,430 --> 00:05:23,490
- Let's go together.
- It's fine.

85
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,830
The factory manager
might be a bit rough,

86
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:27,430
but when it comes to work,

87
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:28,570
he's much more meticulous
than others.

88
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,070
I can handle it on my own.

89
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:34,470
It's not that I don't trust you,

90
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:36,970
but we also need to check
the machinery.

91
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:40,410
It's better to go as a pair
than alone.

92
00:05:40,610 --> 00:05:42,380
Then Young Ung can go with her.

93
00:05:43,050 --> 00:05:44,650
You don't have other work
this afternoon.

94
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,350
No, I don't.

95
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:48,920
Good, then Young Ung will go.

96
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:51,290
Sure, I'll go with him.

97
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,030
Welcome...

98
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:13,340
Mom, the package finally arrived!

99
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:14,780
Hurry and put this together for me.

100
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,280
Hey, Teun Teun.

101
00:06:16,910 --> 00:06:18,050
What's that?

102
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:22,850
It's a robot. Mom promised
to put it together for me today.

103
00:06:23,390 --> 00:06:24,520
Mom, come on.

104
00:06:24,790 --> 00:06:26,360
I'll do it at home later.

105
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:28,290
Why can't you do it now?

106
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,090
There's no one here anyway.

107
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,330
I said I'll do it when we get home.

108
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:34,670
That's going to be too late.

109
00:06:34,730 --> 00:06:36,870
Do it now, please.

110
00:06:36,870 --> 00:06:38,000
Seo Teun Teun.

111
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:40,770
I said I'll do it when we get home.

112
00:06:41,810 --> 00:06:43,040
All right.

113
00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:50,350
What is it? Let me help instead.

114
00:06:50,650 --> 00:06:52,780
- Really?
- Of course.

115
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:55,650
Stuff like this is easy for me.

116
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:57,260
You're so cool.

117
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:59,120
Then you do it for me.

118
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:01,560
All right, shall we begin?

119
00:07:11,070 --> 00:07:12,800
- Teun Teun.
- Yes?

120
00:07:13,670 --> 00:07:16,810
Sometimes at kindergarten,
don't you want to play alone?

121
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:19,180
I do.

122
00:07:19,810 --> 00:07:23,350
When I want to,
I get away from my friends and read.

123
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:25,950
Adults are the same.

124
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:29,420
Sometimes adults need some time
to themselves, too.

125
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:32,220
Then I bet you hate being disturbed
at those times.

126
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:35,890
Yes, I won't even speak
to my friends then.

127
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:39,460
I'm sure it's the same for your mom.

128
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:44,300
On days like that, it's not because
she doesn't like you,

129
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:46,840
and it's not because
you didn't listen to her.

130
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:49,910
It's just one of those days.

131
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:55,110
So on days like today,
when your mom wants to be alone,

132
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:56,450
you can play with me.

133
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,050
Can I really play with you?

134
00:07:59,050 --> 00:08:00,350
Of course.

135
00:08:00,820 --> 00:08:03,620
Want to go to my place
and assemble this robot today?

136
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:04,660
Sounds great!

137
00:08:11,130 --> 00:08:13,630
But why is this so complicated?

138
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:16,100
I take back
saying it's a piece of cake.

139
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,440
Why is this so complicated?

140
00:08:22,610 --> 00:08:24,910
Toys weren't like this
back when I was raising you.

141
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:26,910
You were young back then, Dad.

142
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:29,550
You're right.
But how am I supposed...

143
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:32,180
to assemble this when I can
barely read the instructions?

144
00:08:34,190 --> 00:08:35,190
What are you two doing?

145
00:08:35,690 --> 00:08:38,560
We're assembling this robot
for Teun Teun.

146
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,460
Why would you be doing that?

147
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:44,060
I offered.

148
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,130
This is what uncles usually do.

149
00:08:46,330 --> 00:08:47,770
It's not like he doesn't have one.

150
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:51,800
And why do you keep
getting attached to her son?

151
00:08:51,970 --> 00:08:54,810
That woman is already
crazy about you.

152
00:08:55,970 --> 00:08:57,170
No, she's not.

153
00:08:58,140 --> 00:09:00,650
You always make things up, Grandma.

154
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:04,320
Your grandson isn't that popular.

155
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:08,120
And besides,
even though the boss is single,

156
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:09,690
she actually has high standards.

157
00:09:09,690 --> 00:09:12,660
She has high standards,
which is why she's after you.

158
00:09:12,890 --> 00:09:15,090
Besides, no single mother...

159
00:09:15,130 --> 00:09:17,260
would turn down a man
who adores her child.

160
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:19,360
If you put this much effort
into adoring him,

161
00:09:19,430 --> 00:09:20,970
she'll go even crazier for you.

162
00:09:23,070 --> 00:09:24,300
Put it away!

163
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:30,580
Grandma, you broke it.

164
00:09:30,810 --> 00:09:32,580
After all we did to put it together?

165
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:36,480
I feel like my own leg is broken.

166
00:09:38,050 --> 00:09:39,050
My legs fell asleep.

167
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:45,520
I've got a cramp.
Eun Guk, help me out.

168
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,600
Bye.

169
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:05,410
Boss, are you okay?

170
00:10:23,530 --> 00:10:24,930
I was a little surprised earlier.

171
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:27,400
I didn't expect you
to suggest getting drinks.

172
00:10:28,370 --> 00:10:29,500
Did that turn you off?

173
00:10:29,970 --> 00:10:31,840
No, I didn't mind it at all.

174
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:34,370
Rather than just eating,

175
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:36,840
grabbing a drink lets us have
a deeper conversation.

176
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,780
I can do that completely sober.

177
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:43,380
Eun Seol,

178
00:10:43,650 --> 00:10:45,320
you must be quite curious about me.

179
00:10:46,650 --> 00:10:48,390
What do you want to know?

180
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:51,520
Go on. Lay it on me.

181
00:10:51,690 --> 00:10:53,460
I'll answer you...

182
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:56,130
honestly and sincerely.

183
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,970
Can you really be completely honest?

184
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:06,870
Yes, of course. Ask me anything.

185
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:12,240
Director Joo Mi Ran.

186
00:11:15,850 --> 00:11:19,780
Do you know where she stands
on our scholarship program?

187
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:26,820
Of course she supports it.

188
00:11:28,090 --> 00:11:30,060
From what I've seen
working by her side,

189
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:34,100
she truly respects the Chairman.

190
00:11:35,270 --> 00:11:36,870
If it's what the Chairman wants,

191
00:11:37,230 --> 00:11:38,740
she's the type
to go along with all of it.

192
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:58,660
I see. I figured as much.

193
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,860
The two of them
care for each other so much.

194
00:12:01,690 --> 00:12:04,030
If it's something Ms. Joo orders,

195
00:12:04,430 --> 00:12:06,530
I plan to get it done.

196
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:10,470
Even if it's the wrong thing to do.

197
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:15,570
Abandoned children...

198
00:12:16,210 --> 00:12:18,340
never truly forget the first time...

199
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:21,150
they were held.

200
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:26,680
The person
who first held me like that...

201
00:12:28,490 --> 00:12:29,820
was Ms. Joo.

202
00:12:31,590 --> 00:12:34,390
She might not remember it
as clearly,

203
00:12:34,830 --> 00:12:36,630
but on my first day
at the orphanage,

204
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:38,760
as I wept in the corner,

205
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:42,470
she wrapped me in a warm embrace.

206
00:12:43,630 --> 00:12:46,740
After that, she also provided
continuous financial support.

207
00:12:50,470 --> 00:12:52,010
To repay that favor,

208
00:12:52,940 --> 00:12:54,110
I have to do my best.

209
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:00,250
Even if helping the Director...

210
00:13:01,290 --> 00:13:02,920
is the wrong thing to do,

211
00:13:05,190 --> 00:13:06,460
will you stick by her?

212
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:07,760
Yes.

213
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:10,130
I think I will for now.

214
00:13:11,130 --> 00:13:12,400
No matter what it is.

215
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:30,810
Look at them hanging out
even outside of work.

216
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:35,750
- Let's go somewhere else.
- Why?

217
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,250
Let's just drink here.

218
00:13:40,290 --> 00:13:43,130
First Ko Eun Seol was clinging
to Mr. Seo,

219
00:13:43,390 --> 00:13:45,130
and now she's messing around
with the new secretary?

220
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:49,570
She was definitely born
with a talent for seducing men.

221
00:13:50,530 --> 00:13:51,740
It's impressive.

222
00:13:54,310 --> 00:13:55,370
Let's just go.

223
00:13:56,110 --> 00:13:57,310
Wait for me.

224
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:12,890
Mr. Seok Jin.

225
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:16,230
What is it, Mom?
Did you have another bad dream?

226
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:20,000
Yes. I'm scared.

227
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,430
Let's go. I'll tuck you in.

228
00:14:49,290 --> 00:14:51,100
You won't be too late today, right?

229
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:54,730
Seok Jin has been looking forward
to this play so much.

230
00:14:54,870 --> 00:14:57,470
I'll check out the factory today
and head straight home.

231
00:14:58,070 --> 00:15:00,600
Are you sure? You promised.

232
00:15:01,070 --> 00:15:03,410
Get ready with Seok Jin
and wait for me.

233
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:05,510
- I'll be home early.
- Okay.

234
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:06,940
Have a good day, honey.

235
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:12,950
Honey, what's taking you so long?

236
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:15,390
Seok Jin's really angry right now.

237
00:15:16,090 --> 00:15:19,260
I know. I'm sorry about that.
Just hang on a little longer.

238
00:15:20,560 --> 00:15:21,590
Okay.

239
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:23,130
Kang Young Hoon!

240
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:24,930
That's enough.

241
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:27,260
You're going to get
into serious trouble.

242
00:15:27,970 --> 00:15:29,300
Let go of me.

243
00:15:29,530 --> 00:15:31,600
Just keep your mouth shut
and everything will be fine.

244
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:35,070
Hello?

245
00:15:35,910 --> 00:15:39,240
Honey, what's going on?
Can you hear me?

246
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:42,550
Hello? Honey? Seong Woo!

247
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,930
(Cheongma)

248
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:03,270
Were you
with Secretary Choi yesterday?

249
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:05,940
Yes, how did you know?

250
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:07,370
I just happened to see you.

251
00:16:09,170 --> 00:16:10,340
Are you two close?

252
00:16:10,570 --> 00:16:12,880
We got acquainted while working
on the scholarship program.

253
00:16:14,710 --> 00:16:16,680
Being seen together like that
could hurt your reputation.

254
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,250
Since you're both new here,
you should be mindful of that.

255
00:16:20,650 --> 00:16:22,220
If that reputation...

256
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:25,890
comes from people whispering
and gossiping behind my back,

257
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:28,130
I couldn't care less.

258
00:16:28,930 --> 00:16:30,730
Besides, I'm open to office romance.

259
00:16:32,130 --> 00:16:33,300
What, office romance?

260
00:16:34,230 --> 00:16:35,230
Yes.

261
00:16:35,370 --> 00:16:36,700
I shouldn't let
a good person slip away...

262
00:16:36,770 --> 00:16:38,640
over concerns about my reputation.

263
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,400
So,

264
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:44,040
there's no need to worry, sir.

265
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:48,180
Right, I was worrying for nothing.

266
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:51,880
I'll get back to work then.

267
00:16:52,180 --> 00:16:54,820
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

268
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:02,030
(Planning Director's Office)

269
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:10,430
Why are you down
as the head of finances...

270
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:12,670
for the scholarship foundation?

271
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:15,640
That was an order from the CEO.

272
00:17:15,940 --> 00:17:17,940
He wanted me to thoroughly check...

273
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:20,810
if anything was left out
during the budget execution process.

274
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:24,550
Why are you taking orders from him
regarding the foundation's work?

275
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:26,850
Excuse me?

276
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:28,820
I'm clearly the one...

277
00:17:28,820 --> 00:17:31,560
with the final say
on foundation matters.

278
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:33,760
You should've told me beforehand.

279
00:17:35,190 --> 00:17:36,390
I apologize.

280
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:39,960
I thought you and the CEO
had already agreed on it.

281
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,130
Do you honestly think...

282
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:43,970
I'd give you
the finance team's work as well?

283
00:17:45,070 --> 00:17:47,040
You're already busy enough as it is.

284
00:17:48,110 --> 00:17:50,340
Unbelievable.
He really has no common sense.

285
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,240
I'm sorry, Director Joo.

286
00:17:52,410 --> 00:17:56,950
I'll make sure to tell my husband
to lighten your workload.

287
00:17:58,820 --> 00:18:00,750
Thank you for your concern, ma'am.

288
00:18:02,020 --> 00:18:03,020
It's nothing.

289
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:05,260
You're one of my people,

290
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:07,220
so of course
I should look out for you.

291
00:18:09,890 --> 00:18:11,600
So that's how you want to play it?

292
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:15,230
Then I should make my move, too.

293
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:20,240
How about I stir things up
and really make your blood boil?

294
00:18:21,810 --> 00:18:22,870
Kim Jung Sun.

295
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:25,480
I haven't even started yet.

296
00:19:14,290 --> 00:19:15,890
What are you doing here?

297
00:19:17,090 --> 00:19:18,860
I was just dropping this off.

298
00:19:21,330 --> 00:19:22,330
What's that?

299
00:19:23,170 --> 00:19:24,170
Right.

300
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:28,070
Director Joo asked me
to deliver this to you.

301
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:31,340
Director Joo?

302
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:32,680
Yes.

303
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:35,410
Why would Director Joo give me this?

304
00:19:35,910 --> 00:19:38,980
To thank you for helping Ms. Ko.

305
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:42,620
She's giving me this
to thank me for that?

306
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:45,460
There should be a memo
that Ms. Joo wrote.

307
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:47,090
You should check it.

308
00:19:49,430 --> 00:19:50,430
Secretary Choi.

309
00:19:52,430 --> 00:19:53,830
Whatever the reason,

310
00:19:54,430 --> 00:19:57,030
it's inappropriate
to walk into an office...

311
00:19:58,500 --> 00:19:59,770
when no one's inside.

312
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:03,840
I hope this doesn't happen again.

313
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:05,240
I'm sorry.

314
00:20:05,810 --> 00:20:07,140
I'll be more careful from now on.

315
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:24,960
Mr. Seo,

316
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:27,700
I heard you've been
helping Eun Seol.

317
00:20:28,270 --> 00:20:29,770
Eun Seol is my friend's daughter,

318
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:31,470
so I couldn't help
but always worry about her.

319
00:20:31,770 --> 00:20:34,840
I'm grateful to know
you're looking out for her.

320
00:20:37,740 --> 00:20:39,740
So this is how you threaten me?

321
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:56,530
Did I leave this on earlier?

322
00:21:00,530 --> 00:21:01,530
Darn it.

323
00:21:01,670 --> 00:21:02,670
Just...

324
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,700
Are you still working on that?

325
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:10,010
No, don't. Don't touch it.

326
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:13,080
I'm almost done with this.

327
00:21:13,140 --> 00:21:14,480
Want me to knock it all over?

328
00:21:15,310 --> 00:21:18,320
Why are you driving me crazy too?

329
00:21:18,850 --> 00:21:22,990
Seriously, why are you trying
so hard to impress the landlady?

330
00:21:23,620 --> 00:21:27,320
Seeing that woman look at Eun Guk
makes my stomach turn.

331
00:21:28,790 --> 00:21:30,330
I have my reasons, you know.

332
00:21:31,030 --> 00:21:33,400
Reasons, my foot. As if.

333
00:21:33,460 --> 00:21:34,830
This isn't for Eun Guk.

334
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:37,600
If I pull this off, maybe...

335
00:21:37,970 --> 00:21:40,000
she'll cook us a meal later.

336
00:21:40,070 --> 00:21:43,040
I can't get enough
of Teun Teun's mom's DS.

337
00:21:44,310 --> 00:21:45,310
DS?

338
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:47,810
Doenjang stew.

339
00:21:48,410 --> 00:21:49,410
Doenjang...

340
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:51,880
There we go.

341
00:21:52,780 --> 00:21:53,850
That part is done.

342
00:21:54,690 --> 00:21:56,920
So, what exactly are we assembling?

343
00:22:03,190 --> 00:22:06,100
Here. It's finally finished.

344
00:22:06,130 --> 00:22:08,930
This is exhausting. My back hurts.

345
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:12,570
Don't ever bring
something like this again.

346
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:13,640
My eyes.

347
00:22:14,170 --> 00:22:15,870
My poor eyes.

348
00:22:17,410 --> 00:22:20,880
You're so distracted by dating
that your work's a mess.

349
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:22,780
Redo it.

350
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:27,980
Please let me know
exactly what's missing.

351
00:22:28,290 --> 00:22:30,750
I'll make the changes
and bring you a revision.

352
00:22:31,990 --> 00:22:34,020
I don't like
a single thing about it.

353
00:22:34,620 --> 00:22:36,030
Redo the whole thing from scratch.

354
00:22:37,030 --> 00:22:38,530
If this is how it'll be,

355
00:22:38,530 --> 00:22:40,060
I'll have to assume
you're judging my work...

356
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:43,230
by personal preference
instead of an objective evaluation.

357
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:44,970
You're right.
It's my personal taste.

358
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,040
I have the final say on the design,

359
00:22:48,410 --> 00:22:50,470
so shouldn't my taste be reflected?

360
00:22:51,340 --> 00:22:53,940
The problem is that
your taste keeps changing.

361
00:22:54,810 --> 00:22:56,050
And deciding the design...

362
00:22:56,150 --> 00:22:58,550
for our next season
based purely on personal taste...

363
00:22:58,620 --> 00:22:59,950
seems like a bit of a problem.

364
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,450
If it's a matter of taste,
who could be worse than you?

365
00:23:03,990 --> 00:23:05,790
Your taste is completely unbearable.

366
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:07,420
Excuse me?

367
00:23:07,460 --> 00:23:09,330
I mean your taste in men.

368
00:23:10,130 --> 00:23:12,060
You went after Seok Jin,
and when that failed,

369
00:23:12,130 --> 00:23:13,630
now you're hitting on
the new secretary.

370
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Right?

371
00:23:17,770 --> 00:23:20,470
Yes. But at least I actually try.

372
00:23:21,170 --> 00:23:22,410
I'm nothing like you,

373
00:23:22,410 --> 00:23:24,340
who doesn't even know
how to try in the first place.

374
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:27,880
I'll bring a new design draft.

375
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:39,760
Ms. Joo, did you know?

376
00:23:40,120 --> 00:23:42,630
I think Secretary Choi
and Ko Eun Seol are dating.

377
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:46,200
Who said they are dating?

378
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:48,730
The other day, I saw them
drinking together at a bar.

379
00:23:48,730 --> 00:23:50,230
Totally busted.

380
00:23:50,830 --> 00:23:54,070
It seems like Ko Eun Seol will flirt
with just about anyone.

381
00:23:54,370 --> 00:23:57,040
What a total flirt.
She's a complete vixen.

382
00:23:58,440 --> 00:23:59,480
Do you think...

383
00:24:00,140 --> 00:24:03,550
that you and Ko Eun Seol
are even on the same level?

384
00:24:03,810 --> 00:24:06,050
Of course not.
That goes without saying.

385
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:09,520
Then why do you get so worked up
over every little thing about her?

386
00:24:09,990 --> 00:24:12,920
Chief Cha has completely
made up his mind about you now.

387
00:24:14,260 --> 00:24:18,700
At times like this, I want you
to focus more on your work.

388
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:23,530
You should also start planning
a new program...

389
00:24:23,530 --> 00:24:24,800
for the scholarship foundation.

390
00:24:26,300 --> 00:24:28,100
You want me to help out
with the foundation too?

391
00:24:28,210 --> 00:24:30,410
No way. Why would I do that?

392
00:24:31,010 --> 00:24:33,380
Cheongma's roots lie
in the scholarship foundation.

393
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:36,310
While corporate management
is currently the main priority,

394
00:24:36,650 --> 00:24:39,320
the scholarship foundation remains
at the core of Cheongma.

395
00:24:40,150 --> 00:24:43,520
The position you need to inherit
is the chair of the foundation.

396
00:24:43,820 --> 00:24:45,020
You're telling me to do...

397
00:24:45,090 --> 00:24:46,860
both the design work
and the foundation work?

398
00:24:47,490 --> 00:24:49,030
If Ko Eun Seol can do it,

399
00:24:49,630 --> 00:24:50,930
why can't you?

400
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:53,660
You're right.
If Ko Eun Seol can do it,

401
00:24:54,260 --> 00:24:55,670
I can obviously do it too.

402
00:24:55,930 --> 00:24:58,270
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

403
00:25:00,970 --> 00:25:02,940
I should be careful
around Secretary Choi?

404
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:05,610
Yes. For now,
don't get too close to him.

405
00:25:06,140 --> 00:25:07,880
He doesn't seem like a good person.

406
00:25:09,650 --> 00:25:12,520
Can I ask why you think
that way about him?

407
00:25:13,080 --> 00:25:15,650
You wouldn't say that
without a good reason.

408
00:25:18,050 --> 00:25:19,620
As Director Joo's
executive secretary,

409
00:25:19,820 --> 00:25:21,590
helping her makes sense,

410
00:25:22,630 --> 00:25:23,860
but under the guise
of taking orders,

411
00:25:24,090 --> 00:25:25,900
he seems to cross line after line.

412
00:25:27,230 --> 00:25:29,070
Like what, for example?

413
00:25:32,540 --> 00:25:35,170
Just know that he's someone
you need to be careful of for now.

414
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:37,710
I'll tell you when I'm more certain.

415
00:25:38,170 --> 00:25:39,180
Okay.

416
00:25:39,380 --> 00:25:40,640
The same goes for Ms. Joo.

417
00:25:41,910 --> 00:25:45,080
I think it's best to keep
your distance from Ms. Joo for now.

418
00:25:45,620 --> 00:25:47,050
Just because
she's your mother's friend...

419
00:25:47,120 --> 00:25:48,720
doesn't mean you should
let your guard down.

420
00:25:50,190 --> 00:25:53,820
Actually, she's seemed
a bit different lately.

421
00:25:54,490 --> 00:25:55,990
I happened to overhear this,

422
00:25:55,990 --> 00:25:57,560
but it sounds like she's opposed
to the scholarship program...

423
00:25:57,630 --> 00:25:59,130
I'm trying to push through.

424
00:25:59,730 --> 00:26:00,730
Is that so?

425
00:26:02,130 --> 00:26:04,370
She's not someone
you should just view as an ally.

426
00:26:06,600 --> 00:26:08,540
I'll look into it further,

427
00:26:08,970 --> 00:26:11,070
so keep your guard up.

428
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:12,680
Okay.

429
00:26:18,620 --> 00:26:19,650
(Joo Mi Ran's Past Hospital Records)

430
00:26:19,750 --> 00:26:21,450
(Joo Ae Sook, Taeseon Hospital,
Discharged after giving birth)

431
00:26:29,130 --> 00:26:30,130
(Joo Mi Ran, Na Tae Hoon)

432
00:26:30,430 --> 00:26:33,600
Chief Cha and So Yeon
are coming over tomorrow?

433
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,070
Yes.

434
00:26:35,830 --> 00:26:39,500
I don't even know how long it's been
since we had a meal with So Yeon.

435
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:42,440
It feels like
it's been over 20 years.

436
00:26:43,170 --> 00:26:45,540
You must have been quite close...

437
00:26:45,810 --> 00:26:47,340
before Chief Cha's father
passed away.

438
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:48,450
We were.

439
00:26:48,550 --> 00:26:51,850
His father was
Young Hoon's closest friend.

440
00:26:53,550 --> 00:26:55,390
After what happened to Seong Woo,

441
00:26:56,090 --> 00:26:58,420
So Yeon's mental state deteriorated
from the shock,

442
00:26:59,520 --> 00:27:02,490
so it wasn't easy for us
to see her either.

443
00:27:03,130 --> 00:27:08,130
We intentionally kept our distance,
fearing we'd only hurt each other.

444
00:27:09,100 --> 00:27:10,330
I see.

445
00:27:11,940 --> 00:27:15,740
But now that Chief Cha
and Hae Ra are together,

446
00:27:16,040 --> 00:27:18,480
it's lifted a huge weight
off my chest.

447
00:27:19,340 --> 00:27:21,640
Having Chief Cha join our family
means we can finally...

448
00:27:21,710 --> 00:27:23,580
take care of So Yeon,
who was left completely alone.

449
00:27:23,580 --> 00:27:25,080
What a relief.

450
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:26,950
Right, honey?

451
00:27:28,320 --> 00:27:30,420
Yes, of course.

452
00:27:31,920 --> 00:27:35,030
I really want to get along
with So Yeon.

453
00:27:36,190 --> 00:27:38,130
Once Hae Ra and Chief Cha
get married,

454
00:27:38,500 --> 00:27:41,200
I hope we can be as close
as we used to be.

455
00:27:42,130 --> 00:27:44,230
If we really become in-laws,

456
00:27:44,230 --> 00:27:45,740
we should keep our distance
even more.

457
00:27:46,300 --> 00:27:47,770
When in-laws get too close,

458
00:27:47,770 --> 00:27:49,470
it only leads to trouble.

459
00:27:49,610 --> 00:27:51,840
Is that a rule or something?

460
00:27:52,210 --> 00:27:55,050
So Yeon and the rest of us
were really close.

461
00:27:56,010 --> 00:27:57,410
When the kids get married,

462
00:27:57,680 --> 00:28:02,050
I'm going to go shopping
and travel with So Yeon.

463
00:28:11,090 --> 00:28:12,100
Mr. Seok Jin.

464
00:28:13,200 --> 00:28:14,960
I finished folding your clothes.

465
00:28:15,730 --> 00:28:16,730
Thanks, Mom.

466
00:28:17,500 --> 00:28:18,500
Mom.

467
00:28:19,170 --> 00:28:20,170
Yes?

468
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:22,270
We're going to Hae Ra's house
together tomorrow.

469
00:28:24,540 --> 00:28:26,280
Why would we go there?

470
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:29,450
Hae Ra's parents invited us over.

471
00:28:30,310 --> 00:28:31,650
I don't want to go.

472
00:28:32,720 --> 00:28:34,920
Why? Let's go eat some good food...

473
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:37,190
and have a fun chat
with her parents.

474
00:28:38,050 --> 00:28:40,520
You and Hae Ra's mom
used to be close.

475
00:28:41,120 --> 00:28:44,390
I don't know.
I really don't remember that.

476
00:28:51,770 --> 00:28:54,640
If you keep seeing her,
it'll start coming back to you.

477
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:59,610
It's Hae Ra I don't like,

478
00:29:00,380 --> 00:29:02,080
which makes me want to go even less.

479
00:29:03,510 --> 00:29:05,420
Mom, you're a good person.

480
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:08,650
Could you find it in your heart
to give Hae Ra a chance?

481
00:29:12,320 --> 00:29:13,490
What should we wear tomorrow?

482
00:29:14,290 --> 00:29:16,730
How about that pretty dress
you like so much?

483
00:29:21,630 --> 00:29:23,700
So Yeon, please dig in.

484
00:29:24,030 --> 00:29:26,700
We tried to prepare a lot,
but it feels like it isn't enough.

485
00:29:27,900 --> 00:29:31,040
Not at all.
This looks like more than enough.

486
00:29:31,740 --> 00:29:34,310
Yes, I even helped out
especially for today.

487
00:29:36,250 --> 00:29:37,250
Now, let's eat.

488
00:29:40,050 --> 00:29:42,920
Please try some of this, Mother.

489
00:29:43,690 --> 00:29:45,560
I used a recipe
I learned in my cooking class...

490
00:29:46,190 --> 00:29:47,960
and marinated this bulgogi myself.

491
00:29:49,130 --> 00:29:50,130
Okay.

492
00:29:54,300 --> 00:29:55,330
Here.

493
00:30:00,900 --> 00:30:04,670
What's wrong? You should try some.
Hae Ra made this herself.

494
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:07,440
It's terrible.

495
00:30:18,350 --> 00:30:21,560
So Yeon, please have some tea first.

496
00:30:22,030 --> 00:30:24,360
Hae Ra will bring out the fruit.

497
00:30:24,830 --> 00:30:26,800
Since you were coming over today,

498
00:30:26,860 --> 00:30:29,100
Hae Ra is doing all kinds of things
she never usually does.

499
00:30:34,440 --> 00:30:36,210
It's okay, Director Joo.
I'll go to her.

500
00:30:37,040 --> 00:30:38,040
Just a moment.

501
00:30:44,780 --> 00:30:49,450
Here, please try this.
It was freshly baked this morning.

502
00:30:50,450 --> 00:30:51,790
Thank you.

503
00:30:56,460 --> 00:30:57,560
You haven't...

504
00:30:58,130 --> 00:30:59,760
really changed at all, So Yeon.

505
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:05,370
When Seong Woo was still alive,
we used to meet up quite often.

506
00:31:07,540 --> 00:31:12,180
After all, he was the only friend
I could truly open up to.

507
00:31:13,480 --> 00:31:14,480
Seong Woo and I...

508
00:31:15,280 --> 00:31:17,410
were the best of friends.

509
00:31:19,950 --> 00:31:21,020
You weren't.

510
00:31:23,790 --> 00:31:25,490
I remember everything.

511
00:31:26,390 --> 00:31:28,890
On the day my husband died,

512
00:31:29,630 --> 00:31:32,560
you were shouting at him.

513
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:35,230
You yelled at him,
saying he just needed...

514
00:31:35,230 --> 00:31:36,630
to shut his mouth.

515
00:32:12,770 --> 00:32:16,540
(A Trap Called Desire)

516
00:32:16,710 --> 00:32:19,640
Kang Young Hoon
is definitely hiding something.

517
00:32:19,710 --> 00:32:22,110
Should I try coming up
with a scholarship program too?

518
00:32:22,180 --> 00:32:24,550
It's time I start learning
the foundation's work too.

519
00:32:24,710 --> 00:32:27,480
I was hoping you and Hae Ra
would get engaged.

520
00:32:27,580 --> 00:32:30,590
That's the only way to pass
the scholarship program.

521
00:32:30,650 --> 00:32:33,560
Do you have some special plan
